pocket-motion-only: `<Path>` and its utilities declare an outline that only 0042's PATH op draws; on an upstream target the props would select a table entry no backend renders, so the declaration ships with the op or not at all.

0043 — vector paths, the declaration: `<Path d viewBox>`, the build that
bakes its outline into 0042's PATH TABLE, the utilities and the keyframe
names. The design is `patches/0042-vector-paths.design.md`.

What the patch adds, by file:

- `framework/compiler/path-data.ts` (new): the whole SVG path grammar —
  implicit repeats, exponents, arc flags with no separator, a number after
  `Z` refused rather than read — normalised to move, line, cubic and close:
  relative to absolute, `H`/`V` to lines, `S`/`T` by reflection, `Q` by exact
  degree elevation, every subpath after a close reopened by a move. An arc
  becomes cubics of at most 45 degrees without a transcendental: SVG's
  centre construction, then unit-vector bisection and square roots, with the
  handle length `4/3 tan(a/4)` from two half-angle steps; the x-axis rotation
  the author wrote goes through `cosSinDeg`, exact at multiples of 90 and a
  Taylor series in f64 elsewhere. `compilePathEntry` aligns morph keys — a
  line against a cubic is promoted with controls at 1/3 and 2/3, any other
  difference is refused naming the first differing command and the source
  command each came from — and parses a viewBox.
- `framework/compiler/jsx-plugin.ts`: the collector records `pathDecls`, the
  `d` of every JSX element (any element, so a component forwarding it to a
  `<Path>` is baked from its call site) whose value it can read — a string,
  a backtick with nothing interpolated, a `+` of two, an array of them, a
  `const` of any of those, an element of a `const` array by literal index,
  the parameter of a `.map` callback over one, and the arms of a ternary,
  `||`, `??` and the right of `&&` — paired with the `viewBox` on the same
  element. A `d` it cannot read records nothing. The field rides in the
  transform cache entry, whose file is in the cache key.
- `tools/build.ts`: one PATH TABLE entry per distinct `d` and viewBox,
  baked before the styles; a refusal is `file:line:col: <Path> d does not
  bake: …` and exit 1.
- `framework/compiler/tailwind.ts`: `fill-<color>`, `fill-[#hex]`,
  `fill-none`, `fill-nonzero|evenodd`, `stroke-<color>`, `stroke-none`,
  `stroke-N`, `stroke-[Npx]`, `stroke-join-*`, `stroke-cap-*`,
  `stroke-miter-[N]` (N >= 1), `trim-start-[f]`, `trim-end-[f]`,
  `trim-offset-[f]`, `trim-each|whole`, `morph-[f]` (f >= 0) and
  `bg-clip-path`, which takes the paint path over a legacy two-stop gradient
  as `bg-clip-text` does; `compileClasses` writes the entries into
  styles.bin and `generateStylesModule` writes `PATH_IDS`.
- `framework/compiler/animation.ts`: keyframe names `fillColor`, `fill`,
  `strokeColor`, `stroke`, `strokeWidth` (and `stroke-width`), `trimStart`,
  `trimEnd`, `trimOffset`, `morph`. `stroke-dashoffset` is not one: it is a
  length, and trim a fraction.
- `framework/src/path-key.ts` (new), `primitives.ts`, `components.ts`:
  `Path` is a View that hands the host one attribute, `path`, the key
  `pathKey(d, viewBox)` — the one function the build also keys by — so the
  order `d` and `viewBox` arrive in cannot matter. `native-tree.ts` resolves
  it through `styles.ts`'s `resolvePath` and sets PROP.path; on a strict host
  an unknown key throws naming the outline, on a native host it counts
  `missCounters.unknownPath`. `styles.generated.ts` carries an empty
  `PATH_IDS`, and `index.ts`, `index-octane.ts` and `index-vue-vapor.ts`
  register it at mount as they register `STYLE_IDS`.

